### Requirement 4: Astro Islands for FeatureGrid (Scroll-Triggered Stagger)

**Current state**: The `FeatureGrid.astro` component uses a CSS class `stagger-children` defined in `global.css`. This applies `animate-fade-up` with incrementing delays (0ms to 880ms) to all children immediately on page load. The animation fires whether or not the section is in the viewport.

**Goal**: Add scroll-triggered animation so the stagger only fires when the FeatureGrid scrolls into view.

**Architecture Decision**: The context correctly notes that Astro islands with `client:visible` require a UI framework integration (`@astrojs/react`, `@astrojs/preact`, etc.), and the codebase currently has none. The existing interactive components (ScreenshotShowcase, Header) all use vanilla `<script>` tags. Following this established pattern is the right call.

**Approach**: Use a `<script>` tag with `IntersectionObserver` inside `FeatureGrid.astro`. This is idiomatic Astro -- the `<script>` tag is bundled and deduplicated by Astro's build, and it achieves the same "hydrate on visible" effect as `client:visible` without adding a framework dependency.

#### Step 4.1: Update CSS -- Make stagger-children initially hidden and only animate on trigger

**File**: `/Users/4gray/Code/iptvnator/.claude/worktrees/dazzling-lamport/apps/website/src/styles/global.css`

Change the `.stagger-children` rule so items are hidden by default (opacity 0, no animation), and only animate when a `.stagger-visible` class is added to the parent:

```css
.stagger-children > * {
  @apply opacity-0;
}

.stagger-children.stagger-visible > * {
  @apply animate-fade-up;
}
.stagger-children.stagger-visible > *:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 0ms; }
.stagger-children.stagger-visible > *:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 80ms; }
/* ... same pattern through :nth-child(12) ... */
```

#### Step 4.2: Add IntersectionObserver script to FeatureGrid.astro

**File**: `/Users/4gray/Code/iptvnator/.claude/worktrees/dazzling-lamport/apps/website/src/components/FeatureGrid.astro`

Add a `data-stagger` attribute to the grid container (the `div` with `stagger-children` class), then append a `<script>` tag:

On the grid div (line 84):
```html
<div class="stagger-children mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" data-stagger>
```

Script to add at the end of the file:
```html
<script>
  const staggerContainers = document.querySelectorAll('[data-stagger]');

  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add('stagger-visible');
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.1 }
  );

  staggerContainers.forEach((el) => observer.observe(el));
</script>
```

This script:
- Finds all `[data-stagger]` elements (currently just the FeatureGrid)
- Creates a single `IntersectionObserver` with 10% threshold
- When the grid enters the viewport, adds `stagger-visible` to trigger the CSS animations
- Unobserves after triggering (one-shot)

**Note**: This pattern is reusable. Any future component can add `stagger-children` + `data-stagger` to get the same scroll-triggered stagger behavior.

